  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "ca5a648658b278909efcf45b0da5ab407d4001d5",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ca5a648658b278909efcf45b0da5ab407d4001d5",
      "message": "Merge pull request #768 from Anastasia-Labs/codex/fix-751-terminal-removal\n\nReconcile descendant removals after external target cleanup",
      "authorName": "colll78",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T10:14:19Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "02049c3b16ab80d89da71c612214ad78b0301998",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/02049c3b16ab80d89da71c612214ad78b0301998",
      "message": "Reconcile descendant removals after external target cleanup (#751)\n\nAn included descendant peel could remain unresolved when another caller removed the target before its acknowledgement. Confirm the original peel receipt and authenticate the later terminal independently, while refusing completion over unresolved submission intents.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T08:53:46Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b987e6d9ee07139e817c68acd4a05ef5abea4c66",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b987e6d9ee07139e817c68acd4a05ef5abea4c66",
      "message": "Merge pull request #737 from Anastasia-Labs/codex/da-public-candidate\n\nComplete canonical fault-proof recovery and foreign-block verification",
      "authorName": "colll78",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T05:29:10Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c0837efad623cb7f24887b5fde0d8427e283ac0d",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c0837efad623cb7f24887b5fde0d8427e283ac0d",
      "message": "Shrink the workflow size record after parent recovery extraction (#737)\n\nThe required module-size metadata check enforces exact current sizes. Record the smaller 959-line orchestrator after extracting historical-parent reobservation, preserving a stricter cap and the verified runtime source.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T04:10:26Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c86719bd0cb49d4869927ae2108050c57e4fc656",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c86719bd0cb49d4869927ae2108050c57e4fc656",
      "message": "Budget real-contract source fixture setup explicitly (#737)\n\nThe canonical contract and manifest fixture exceeded Vitest's default 10-second setup budget under CI contention. Load the identical contracts once and use the existing same-helper 120-second fixture budget without changing test assertions or global timeouts.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T03:58:15Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4f7c38e787f7fbbe5eea49857a070a3f91fe57ea",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4f7c38e787f7fbbe5eea49857a070a3f91fe57ea",
      "message": "Keep included proof parents closed during descendant recovery (#737)\n\nAn included cancellation can consume a parent's effects before its journal confirmation. Authenticate the historical parent's inclusion without replay authority before reopening its funding and journal, so pending descendants can reconcile. Preserve rollback recovery and signed-intent ownership checks.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T03:50:37Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "877f1673d4c450b9f5fbb4f964ea3ae42166657b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/877f1673d4c450b9f5fbb4f964ea3ae42166657b",
      "message": "Reconcile rolled-back proof parents before pending descendants (#737)\n\nA pending descendant must not suppress reobservation of its previously confirmed parent after rollback. Keep reconciliation first for the current action when its own signed intent is unresolved, and preserve funding collision and authenticated expiry checks. The twelve canonical reobservation cases and the original workflow, cancellation and terminal recovery suites pass.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T02:39:50Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4fd96e816b0c2c10a79187978e25fbb0d0728e11",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4fd96e816b0c2c10a79187978e25fbb0d0728e11",
      "message": "Align recovery fixtures with the canonical root and scheduler (#737)\n\nKeep the SQL adoption fixture connected to its authenticated confirmed root. Refresh the parent scheduler before each bounded commit retry so advancing an emulator slot does not repeatedly invoke the mutation worker with a stale schedule. Preserve the production guards, signed-intent assertions and native recovery paths.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T02:32:59Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "72523d52040a495fb509052ad7bd316b4fae48e6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/72523d52040a495fb509052ad7bd316b4fae48e6",
      "message": "Use typed event-key schemas in fault-proof expectations (#737)\n\nThe raw TypeBox schema inferred its schema shape as the serialized value type and failed the complete fault-proof TypeScript check. Use the existing typed alias of the same runtime schema. The affected two-file selection passes all eight tests and the complete package typecheck passes.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T01:25:36Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "3d9c4c098b7a1e57e42dc5f8766f04c648ab6846",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/3d9c4c098b7a1e57e42dc5f8766f04c648ab6846",
      "message": "Adopt canonical foreign replay and authenticated deposit identity (#737)\n\nEncode native inserts with the shared ledger descriptor converter, compare descriptor replay with independently verified raw ledger entries, and retain authenticated deposit transaction/address identity in SQL. Prove honest foreign-header recovery through actual rebuilt submission and confirmation.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T01:05:21Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "09cba090515edafd7e020fba35181ac374759bb4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/09cba090515edafd7e020fba35181ac374759bb4",
      "message": "Keep removed local roots under correction recovery ownership (#737)\n\nAvoid foreign-adoption work for authenticated local recovery obligations. Bind retained journal or applied signed-release ancestry to the deployment, profile, native binary and current canonical base; preserve closed readiness and unbound-root refusal while ordinary correction recovery completes.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T01:02:25Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "932b35f3d59720c5a3031c6b20475249f652cebd",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/932b35f3d59720c5a3031c6b20475249f652cebd",
      "message": "Verify the current base during signed local continuation (#737)\n\nA landed signed journal can outlive the previous confirmed queue reference. Resolve and authenticate the current canonical tail for pending local finalization while retaining exact signed-journal, native, deployment and source checks on the separately retained continuation.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T00:53:42Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "d239acba97a5ea339d72f2a2581a492cdb57df4e",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/d239acba97a5ea339d72f2a2581a492cdb57df4e",
      "message": "Tighten module caps after recovery fixture reductions (#737)\n\nRefresh the four explicit ceilings to the shorter current files and remove obsolete declaration line counts. No ceiling is raised and no new exception is introduced.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T00:48:55Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "1aad727d4bad94dc1089effb1835212aa09b8f42",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/1aad727d4bad94dc1089effb1835212aa09b8f42",
      "message": "Restore reachable forced-verdict and retained frontier fixtures (#737)\n\nUse individually legal, conserved outputs to exercise aggregate certified carriage, keep oversized output refusal as an explicit first-fault control, and use an accepted native mint trace to prove the complete retained ScriptSources frontier.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T00:38:26Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "40e440859e253c5cb582d3033f0e2f5392ea507e",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/40e440859e253c5cb582d3033f0e2f5392ea507e",
      "message": "Exercise authenticated history and current recovery fixtures (#737)\n\nUse actual paired-history initialization in the pool-isolation regression, provide the runtime Globals dependency, and pin the two new transactional migrations. Verify exact reference-output matching without weakening publication authentication.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-05T00:34:19Z"
    }
